    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Common Examples\n\n| Code | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| FI 001 | Flowmeter - Indicating |\n| TT 001 | Temperature - Transmitter |\n| FV 001 | Control Valve |\n| ZSH 001 | Position Switch - High Level |\n\n## Reference\n\nBased on ANSI/ISA S5.1-1984 (R 1992) \"Instrumentation symbols and identification\"\n\n### Structure\n\n1. **First Letter**: Measured or initiating variable (A-Z)\n2. **Modifier Letter** (Optional): Modifies the first letter (D, F, J, K, M, Q, S, X, Y, Z)\n3. **Second Letter**: Readout, output, or modifier function\n4. **Modifier Function** (Optional): Further modifies the function\n5. **Number**: Sequential or process-line-related identification"
